arguments.prompt:
You are working in /tmp/sv-d448e9a9efe74df6b19bc7d36d519469 which has a Blazor Web App solution (ShipmentTracker.sln) with two projects:
- ShipmentTracker (server) — has EF Core with SQLite, ASP.NET Identity, prerendering
- ShipmentTracker.Client (WebAssembly client) — has pages rendered interactively via WASM

The app uses Global WebAssembly interactivity with prerendering (--all-interactive flag). Authentication is Individual accounts (ASP.NET Core Identity).

## Task

Build a shipment tracking app for a logistics company. Here's what to implement:

### 1. Shared Model (create in ShipmentTracker.Client so both projects can reference it)

Create `ShipmentTracker.Client/Models/Shipment.cs`:
```csharp
namespace ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;

public class Shipment
{
    public int Id { get; set; }
    public string TrackingNumber { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Origin { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Destination { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public ShipmentStatus Status { get; set; }
    public DateTime ShippedDate { get; set; }
    public DateTime EstimatedDelivery { get; set; }
    public string CustomerEmail { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Description { get; set; } = string.Empty;
}

public enum ShipmentStatus
{
    Pending,
    PickedUp,
    InTransit,
    OutForDelivery,
    Delivered,
    Delayed
}
```

### 2. Database (server project)

Update `ShipmentTracker/Data/ApplicationDbContext.cs` to add a DbSet<Shipment> (reference the model from the Client project). Add `using ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;`.

### 3. API Endpoints (server project)

Create `ShipmentTracker/Endpoints/ShipmentEndpoints.cs` with minimal API endpoints:
- `GET /api/shipments` — returns all shipments (requires auth, for dispatchers)
- `GET /api/shipments/{trackingNumber}` — returns a single shipment by tracking number (requires auth)
- `POST /api/shipments` — creates a shipment (requires auth, for dispatchers)
- `PUT /api/shipments/{id}` — updates a shipment (requires auth, for dispatchers)

Register endpoints in Program.cs by calling `app.MapShipmentEndpoints();` before `app.Run();`.

### 4. Client-side Service

Create `ShipmentTracker.Client/Services/ShipmentService.cs`:
```csharp
using System.Net.Http.Json;
using ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;

namespace ShipmentTracker.Client.Services;

public class ShipmentService(HttpClient http)
{
    public async Task<List<Shipment>> GetShipmentsAsync()
        => await http.GetFromJsonAsync<List<Shipment>>("api/shipments") ?? [];

    public async Task<Shipment?> TrackShipmentAsync(string trackingNumber)
    {
        var response = await http.GetAsync($"api/shipments/{trackingNumber}");
        if (!response.IsSuccessStatusCode) return null;
        return await response.Content.ReadFromJsonAsync<Shipment>();
    }

    public async Task<Shipment?> CreateShipmentAsync(Shipment shipment)
    {
        var response = await http.PostAsJsonAsync("api/shipments", shipment);
        if (!response.IsSuccessStatusCode) return null;
        return await response.Content.ReadFromJsonAsync<Shipment>();
    }

    public async Task<bool> UpdateShipmentAsync(Shipment shipment)
    {
        var response = await http.PutAsJsonAsync($"api/shipments/{shipment.Id}", shipment);
        return response.IsSuccessStatusCode;
    }
}
```

Register `ShipmentService` in both `ShipmentTracker.Client/Program.cs` AND `ShipmentTracker/Program.cs` (for prerendering). The HttpClient base address on the server side should be configured properly. 

In the client Program.cs, add:
```csharp
builder.Services.AddScoped<ShipmentService>();
```

In the server Program.cs, add (before `var app = builder.Build();`):
```csharp
builder.Services.AddScoped<ShipmentService>();
builder.Services.AddHttpClient<ShipmentService>(client => 
    client.BaseAddress = new Uri("https://localhost"));
```

Actually, for prerendering with the server, use a simpler approach. Register the service with an HttpClient that has the app's base address. Add this to the server Program.cs:
```csharp
builder.Services.AddHttpClient<ShipmentService>(client =>
{
    client.BaseAddress = new Uri(builder.Configuration["AppBaseUrl"] ?? "https://localhost:5001");
});
```

And in appsettings.Development.json add `"AppBaseUrl": "https://localhost:5001"` (or whatever port is in launchSettings).

Actually the simplest approach for the server-side prerendering registration: just register the ShipmentService with a named HttpClient. Let me simplify:

For the **server** Program.cs, add before `var app`:
```csharp
builder.Services.AddScoped<ShipmentService>();
builder.Services.AddScoped(sp => new HttpClient { BaseAddress = new Uri("https://localhost:7001") });
```

Wait no, the server already makes direct DB calls. A better pattern: create an interface or just have the server endpoints serve data and the client call them. Since prerendering will call the same WASM components, those components need ShipmentService available on the server too. 

The cleanest approach: Register ShipmentService in both projects. For the server, provide an HttpClient that points back to itself. Use `IHttpClientFactory`. Here's what to do:

**Server Program.cs** — add before `var app = builder.Build();`:
```csharp
builder.Services.AddHttpClient<ShipmentService>((sp, client) =>
{
    // During prerendering, the service calls back to itself
    client.BaseAddress = new Uri("https://localhost:7240");
});
```

Check what port the app uses in Properties/launchSettings.json and use that. If there's no launchSettings, just use a configuration-driven approach.

Actually, let's keep it simple and NOT prerender data-fetching pages. The pages can use `@attribute [StreamRendering]` or just load data on the client. Since the render mode is WebAssembly, during prerender the component will just show a loading state and then the WASM runtime takes over and fetches data.

Simplest approach:
- Register `ShipmentService` in Client/Program.cs with the existing HttpClient
- Register `ShipmentService` in Server/Program.cs for prerendering with an HttpClient pointing to itself

Let me check what's in the client Program.cs first and adjust.

Actually, just do this:

**Client/Program.cs** should have HttpClient registered already (check). Add `builder.Services.AddScoped<ShipmentService>();`

**Server/Program.cs**: Add:
```csharp
builder.Services.AddScoped<ShipmentService>();
builder.Services.AddScoped(sp => new HttpClient { BaseAddress = new Uri("http://localhost") });
```

The prerender won't actually fetch data successfully (since the server isn't fully started when prerendering happens for the first request), but that's fine—components should handle null/empty state gracefully and load data once WASM is active.

### 5. Pages (in ShipmentTracker.Client/Pages/)

**Replace** `Home.razor` with a landing page that has a tracking number input for customers:

```razor
@page "/"
@using ShipmentTracker.Client.Models
@using ShipmentTracker.Client.Services
@inject ShipmentService ShipmentService

<PageTitle>ShipmentTracker - Track Your Shipment</PageTitle>

<h1>Track Your Shipment</h1>

<div class="row mb-4">
    <div class="col-md-6">
        <div class="input-group">
            <input type="text" class="form-control" placeholder="Enter tracking number..."
                   @bind="trackingNumber" @bind:event="oninput" @onkeyup="HandleKeyUp" />
            <button class="btn btn-primary" @onclick="TrackShipment" disabled="@isLoading">
                @if (isLoading) { <span class="spinner-border spinner-border-sm me-1"></span> }
                Track
            </button>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

@if (shipment is not null)
{
    <div class="card">
        <div class="card-header">
            <h5>Shipment @shipment.TrackingNumber</h5>
        </div>
        <div class="card-body">
            <dl class="row">
                <dt class="col-sm-3">Status</dt>
                <dd class="col-sm-9"><span class="badge bg-@GetStatusColor(shipment.Status)">@shipment.Status</span></dd>
                <dt class="col-sm-3">Origin</dt>
                <dd class="col-sm-9">@shipment.Origin</dd>
                <dt class="col-sm-3">Destination</dt>
                <dd class="col-sm-9">@shipment.Destination</dd>
                <dt class="col-sm-3">Description</dt>
                <dd class="col-sm-9">@shipment.Description</dd>
                <dt class="col-sm-3">Shipped Date</dt>
                <dd class="col-sm-9">@shipment.ShippedDate.ToString("MMM dd, yyyy")</dd>
                <dt class="col-sm-3">Estimated Delivery</dt>
                <dd class="col-sm-9">@shipment.EstimatedDelivery.ToString("MMM dd, yyyy")</dd>
            </dl>
        </div>
    </div>
}
else if (notFound)
{
    <div class="alert alert-warning">No shipment found with that tracking number.</div>
}

@code {
    private string trackingNumber = string.Empty;
    private Shipment? shipment;
    private bool isLoading;
    private bool notFound;

    private async Task HandleKeyUp(KeyboardEventArgs e)
    {
