## Important notes:
- The Client project already references `Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.WebAssembly` etc.
- The Server project already references the Client project.
- Keep the existing Identity/Account pages intact.
- Use `@attribute [StreamRendering]` is NOT needed since we load data in OnAfterRenderAsync (avoids prerender issues).
- Make sure HttpClient is properly registered in both Program.cs files for the ShipmentService.

For the Client Program.cs, it likely already has an HttpClient registered. Just add:
```csharp
builder.Services.AddScoped<ShipmentService>();
```

For the Server Program.cs add:
```csharp
builder.Services.AddScoped<ShipmentService>();
builder.Services.AddScoped(sp => new HttpClient { BaseAddress = new Uri("http://localhost") });
```

This HttpClient on the server side won't actually be used meaningfully during prerender since data loads in OnAfterRenderAsync (which only fires on the client), but it satisfies DI resolution.
